This kind of information can be captured well by using model representations given by orthonormal basis functions.\\
Any stable transfer function can be represented by the following infinite sum:
\begin{equation}
G(q)=\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}h(k)\mathcal{L}_k(a,q),
\end{equation}
where $q$ is the time shift operator ($qu(t)\doteq u(t+1)$) and $\mathcal{L}_k$ are mutually orthogonal transfer functions characterized by:
\begin{equation}\label{Eq:ortogonality}
\frac{1}{2\pi j}\oint \mathcal{L}_p(a,q)\mathcal{L}_k(a,q^{-1})\frac{dq}{q}=\delta_{pk},
\end{equation}
where $\delta_{pk}$ is the Kronecker delta function and the integral is around the unit circle.

\begin{equation}
